{"caseId":"OD2-HO-STOP-2","methodChoice":"D (competing hypotheses): the evidence already discriminates between the rival explanations, so I collected nothing further.","answers":[{"itemId":"I-H1","answer":"contradicted","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["E3","E2","E1"]},{"itemId":"I-H2","answer":"contradicted","confidence":82,"evidenceIds":["E2","E3"]},{"itemId":"I-H3","answer":"supported","confidence":78,"evidenceIds":["E1","E2","E3"]},{"itemId":"I-H4","answer":"unknown","confidence":70,"evidenceIds":["E6","E2"]},{"itemId":"I-H5","answer":"contradicted","confidence":88,"evidenceIds":["E2","E6"]},{"itemId":"I-R1","answer":"contradicted","confidence":80,"evidenceIds":["E2"]},{"itemId":"I-R2","answer":"causal","confidence":92,"evidenceIds":["E1"]},{"itemId":"I-R3","answer":"contradicted","confidence":72,"evidenceIds":["E5","E3"]},{"itemId":"I-R4","answer":"association-only","confidence":62,"evidenceIds":["E5"]},{"itemId":"I-A1","answer":"preferred","confidence":68,"evidenceIds":["E1","E2","E3"]},{"itemId":"I-A2","answer":"harmful","confidence":85,"evidenceIds":["E3","E2"]},{"itemId":"I-A3","answer":"harmful","confidence":92,"evidenceIds":["E2"]},{"itemId":"I-A4","answer":"premature","confidence":80,"evidenceIds":["E6"]},{"itemId":"I-A5","answer":"acceptable","confidence":65,"evidenceIds":["E2","E6"]},{"itemId":"I-SUFF","answer":"sufficient","confidence":70,"evidenceIds":["E1","E2","E3","E5"]}],"brief":"Analyzer B most likely had a single chance QC outlier. The repeat from the same vial passed. Sodium, chloride and the other two potassium levels were fine. Level 2 means are unchanged since the lot change (5.81 before, 5.80 after). Only one flag appeared in a month, which fits the expected false-rejection rate. B and A agree on 43 patient samples (mean difference +0.02). B's patient median is steady. All 182 scheduled QC runs were completed on time, so the claim that short staffing led to skipped QC is not supported. A short sample or bubble can't be excluded, so don't record it as the confirmed cause.

Ward 6's high potassiums are split evenly between Analyzers A and B. They coincide with the tube outage, which caused long transport delays, and with four renal overflow patients. Delay is the likelier explanation, though that link is only an association so far. No repeat samples were requested.

What to sign off: return B to service and close the 186 results with no amendments. Optionally add extra Level 2 QC for a week. Don't recall results, quarantine the lot or widen the limits. Ask Ward 6 to send repeat samples and fix the tube station. I'm moderately confident in this."}
